The edge-state checks found a substantive error: collections whose coefficient rows are exactly identical can receive tiny positive variances from rounding. With three copies of each of two shapes, the app reports a variance ratio of about 6.33 × 10³¹ instead of saying neither collection varies. I’m documenting that as a blocker, alongside the reporting and test-coverage defects.

